        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Prepared under precautions against oxygen and water, with anhydrous starting materials (detailed procedures also referenced to Wijk et al., 1996). Potassium (12.79 mmol) was dissolved in 2-propanol–toluene, then Ti(OiPr)4 (1.066 mmol) was added. After 2 h, TbCl3 (3.836 mmol) and ErCl3 (0.426 mmol) were added and the mixture was reacted for 3 d at room temperature. The weakly pink solution was separated from precipitated KCl; evaporation of the solution gave pale pink crystals of the title compound.",
